{
  "slug": "keepgoing",
  "name": "Keepgoing",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Session memory for Claude Code automatically saves checkpoints during work, shows what you were doing upon return, and tracks progress across sessions. It includes 7 slash commands for resuming context, saving checkpoints, viewing progress, and exporting context to other AI tools. It also configures session hooks and an MCP server with 12 tools for comprehensive session awareness.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**, **4 hooks** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `briefing` (Use when the user wants a comprehensive context reconstruction before a big session - \"full briefing\", \"catch me…), `handoff` (Use when the user wants to switch to another AI tool (ChatGPT, Gemini, Copilot, etc.) and carry context…), `hot` (Use when the user asks \"what am I working on these days\", \"what's active\", \"show all my projects\",…), `progress` (Use when the user needs a standup update, sprint review summary, \"what did I do this week\", \"summarize…), `reentry` (Use when the user says \"where did I leave off\", \"what was I working on\", \"pick up where…), `save` (Use when the user says \"save a checkpoint\", \"checkpoint\", \"save progress\", \"mark this milestone\", or wants to explicitly…)\n- **Hooks** (4): `SessionStart`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `SessionEnd`\n- **MCP servers** (1): `session`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install keepgoing@claude-community` from `keepgoing-dev/claude-plugin`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 6,
    "hook": 4,
    "mcp": 1
  },
